                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Orbital Injection is a small free sandbox game where you... inject things into orbit!\n\nhttps://youtu.be/LRVHW4NL1xg\n\nIt's a pretty relaxing game. The music, when turned on, is very relaxing. The whole experience is very calming. Sit back. Crack open a cold one and throw planets at a sun.\n\nThere are a few bugs. The last item on your pallet will often be super sized. You have a limited number of items you can spawn from your pallet and as things are destroyed they don't come back so you have to reset.\n\nIt's probably not enough content to warrant the 1.99 price tag but Im still going to give it a positive review. It does exactly what it says it's going to do and in its simplicity, it's actually enjoyable.\n\nUnfortunately even with the super low sound even this got a copyright claim by the asshats over at The Orchard Music on behalf of ant-zen. Not only do they copyright claim licensed music but they don't review/acknowledge disputes. Sorry, /rant.",
